# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. The single most important block in this file.
# .env holds your API keys. A key pushed to public GitHub is found
# by scraper bots within minutes and used until your credits run out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
# The "!" means "except this one". .env.example is the blank
# template with no real values, and it is meant to be committed.
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled bytecode, regenerated automatically on every run.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# The virtual environment: hundreds of MB of installed libraries,
# rebuilt by anyone from requirements.txt in a single command.
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Your personal data. Never committed, not even to a private repo.
# The claim register is the densest description of you that exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under data/ is personal and stays here. A negation cannot
# rescue a file from an excluded *directory*, so this excludes the
# contents rather than the folder itself.
data/*
logs/*
*.db
*.sqlite3

# The one exception: the demo database ships inside the public image. It
# is built by scripts/build_demo_db.py and contains only mode='demo'
# rows, which that script verifies before writing.
!data/demo.db

# The run log is the evidence that the watch ran unattended, and the
# README points a judge at it. Run summaries only, no content.
!logs/monitor.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# OS and editor junk
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# Draft answers for the submission form. Notes to self, not part of
# the project.
SUBMISSION.md
